Error: Jet.RuntimeStringAsCheckedText: A runtime `String` can't be used as `Sh`
  --> Tests/UI/typed_text_runtime_string.jet:6:17
    |
  6 |     run_command(text)
    |                 ^^^^
 Why: `Sh` is checked text, built only from a checked literal whose `{value}` holes its `CheckedText` impl encodes, so untrusted text can't change its meaning
 Fix: Write `Sh{"..."}` with `{value}` holes, or use `Sh.raw("…")` if you have audited the text
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.RuntimeStringAsCheckedText
